# SGI - INE5420 3D sample: a bicubic Bezier surface of 3 patches (trabalho 1.9)
# A wave "terrain" over a 4 x 10 control net: rows at z = -45, -15, 15, 45,
# columns at x = -90..90 in steps of 20, heights y rising and falling along x.
# The patches take columns 1-4, 4-7 and 7-10, sharing their border columns;
# the control points on either side of each join are collinear with it, so
# the patches meet smoothly. Head-on the wave shows in profile; pitch or
# orbit the view to see the mesh.
o terrain
v -90 0 -45
v -70 20 -45
v -50 20 -45
v -30 0 -45
v -10 -20 -45
v 10 -20 -45
v 30 0 -45
v 50 20 -45
v 70 20 -45
v 90 0 -45
v -90 0 -15
v -70 40 -15
v -50 40 -15
v -30 0 -15
v -10 -40 -15
v 10 -40 -15
v 30 0 -15
v 50 40 -15
v 70 40 -15
v 90 0 -15
v -90 0 15
v -70 40 15
v -50 40 15
v -30 0 15
v -10 -40 15
v 10 -40 15
v 30 0 15
v 50 40 15
v 70 40 15
v 90 0 15
v -90 0 45
v -70 20 45
v -50 20 45
v -30 0 45
v -10 -20 45
v 10 -20 45
v 30 0 45
v 50 20 45
v 70 20 45
v 90 0 45
cstype bezier
deg 3 3
surf 0 1 0 1 1 2 3 4 11 12 13 14 21 22 23 24 31 32 33 34
parm u 0 1
parm v 0 1
end
surf 0 1 0 1 4 5 6 7 14 15 16 17 24 25 26 27 34 35 36 37
parm u 0 1
parm v 0 1
end
surf 0 1 0 1 7 8 9 10 17 18 19 20 27 28 29 30 37 38 39 40
parm u 0 1
parm v 0 1
end
